  "description": "Subject: Retrospective Listed Building Consent – 5 Pond Cottages, College Road, Dulwich SE21 7LE\n\n\n\nDear Ms Chapman,\n\n\n\nI hope you are well.\n\n\n\nI am writing regarding the listed building consent application originally submitted in 2007 (Ref: 07/AP/2453) for works to 5 Pond Cottages, College Road, Dulwich SE21 7LE. As you know, I have been in touch a few times about this matter.\n\n\n\nUnfortunately, we naively installed a conservation-style rooflight without realising that separate listed building consent was required. We are now in the process of selling the property and would like to seek retrospective consent for the rooflight installation.\n\n\n\nThis whole process has been extremely stressful for us. We are very passionate about these cottages and, as you know, we also own No. 6 Pond Cottages. We have poured our heart and soul into maintaining and improving both homes in a way that respects their history and setting.\n\n\n\nThe rooflight we installed is a conservation-grade steel unit, positioned on the south-facing slope, where it is not visible from the road. Many of our neighbouring properties have similar rooflights, and we have been careful to ensure ours is in keeping with the character of the building.\n\n\n\nWe are preparing to relaunch the property with a new agent and are concerned that the absence of listed consent could once again jeopardise the sale. I understand the standard determination period is eight weeks, but if there is any way the process could be expedited or if you could advise on any steps we might take to avoid delays, I would be extremely grateful.\n\n\n\nI will send through photographs shortly to support the application. Thank you so much for your time, understanding, and guidance — it is very much appreciated.\n\n\n\nWith best wishes,\n\nJulie \n"
}